{
    "background_story": "Maddox was a majestic Stilt Sandpiper, a member of the stizidae family, known for their remarkable migratory journeys. Born in the Arctic tundra, Maddox spent his summers feasting on insects and small crustaceans in the wetlands. As the seasons changed, he would embark on an epic 9,000-mile journey to his wintering grounds in South America. Maddox's remarkable endurance and navigational skills allowed him to traverse vast expanses of ocean, stopping only to refuel at strategic locations. His striking black and white plumage made him a striking sight among his fellow shorebirds. Despite the perils of his journey, Maddox returned to his Arctic home year after year, a testament to the resilience and determination of these incredible birds.",
